@startuml <SLUG>_UseCase
' =====================================================================
' Use Case Diagram — STARTER TEMPLATE  (Phase 03 Modeling, diagram 1 of 7)
' Builds on: Actors (Phase 01 Stakeholder_Mission) + Functional REQ-F-*
' Conventions §7: notation contract. Replace <PLACEHOLDERS>; delete (example) lines.
' <<include>> = shared sub-flow (always runs);  <<extend>> = optional/exception flow.
' =====================================================================
title <Project Name> — Use Case Diagram (TODO)

left to right direction

' --- Actors (pull from the Phase 01 stakeholder table; do not re-elicit) ---
actor "<Primary Actor>" as PrimaryActor
actor "<Secondary Actor>" as SecondaryActor
' actor "End User" as EndUser   ' (example — delete)

rectangle "<System Name>" {
  usecase "<Primary Goal>" as UC1
  usecase "<Shared Sub-flow>" as UCShared
  usecase "<Optional / Exception Flow>" as UCExt
  ' usecase "Start Session" as UC1   ' (example — delete)
  ' usecase "Authenticate"   as UCShared ' (example — delete)
}

' --- Actor ↔ use case associations ---
PrimaryActor --> UC1
SecondaryActor --> UC1

' --- Relationships between use cases ---
UC1 ..> UCShared : <<include>>
UC1 ..> UCExt    : <<extend>>

' --- Refinement to functional requirements (a use case <<refine>>s a REQ-F-*) ---
' Record which REQ each use case refines (refine = clarifies meaning, REQ↔model element).
note bottom of UC1
  refines REQ-F-<nn>
  TODO: list every REQ-F-* this use case serves
end note

@enduml
